===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|la|nabla}}, from {{bor|en|grc|νάβλα||Phoenician harp}}, from ancient {{der|en|he|נֵבֶל|tr=nḗḇel}} or a {{der|en|phn|-}} cognate. {{dbt|en|nebel}}, which comes via the modern {{m+|he|נֵ֤בֶל}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[Hebrew]] [[stringed instrument]].
# {{lb|en|analysis}} The symbol [[∇]], used to denote the [[gradient]] operator.

